[{"question": "What programs are offered at SPUS? What are the available undergraduate programs? What courses are available?", "answer": "Saint Paul University Surigao (SPUS) offers a comprehensive range of undergraduate programs across five (5) colleges:\n\n**College of Health Sciences (4-Year Curriculum)**\n- Bachelor of Science in Nursing\n- Bachelor of Science in Psychology\n\n**College of Education, Arts and Sciences (3-Year Curriculum)**\n- Bachelor of Arts (Major in: Political Science, Philosophy, English Language, Sociology, Mass Communication)\n- Bachelor of Science in Mathematics\n- Bachelor of Science in Public Administration\n- Bachelor of Elementary Education\n- Bachelor of Secondary Education (Major in: English, Filipino, Mathematics, Sciences, Social Studies, Values Education)\n- Bachelor of Early Childhood Education\n- Bachelor of Physical Education\n\n**College of Business Management and Accountancy (4-Year Curriculum)**\n- Bachelor of Science in Accountancy\n- Bachelor of Science in Business Administration (Major in: Financial Management, Marketing Management, Human Resource Development Management)\n- Bachelor of Science in Hospitality Management\n- Bachelor of Science in Tourism Management\n- Bachelor of Science in Accounting and Information System\n- Bachelor of Science in Office Administration\n\n**College of Engineering & Information Technology (4-Year Curriculum)**\n- Bachelor of Science in Mining Engineering\n- Bachelor of Science in Civil Engineering\n- Bachelor of Science in Computer Engineering\n- Bachelor of Science in Information Technology\n\n**College of Criminal Justice Education (4-Year Curriculum)**\n- Bachelor of Science in Criminology\n- Bachelor of Forensic Science\n\nSPUS also offers Graduate School programs (PhD, Masters) and TVET/TESDA programs. For inquiries, contact the Registrar at registrar@spus.edu.ph or call 09635606094.", "category": "Academics", "source_type": "office", "source_office": "Registrar", "embedding": [-0.03